DESCRIPTION:***************************************************************
 **\nAssignment 1 PART A : Proposals (with selected development model)\n***
 **************************************************************\n\n------\n
 PROMPT\n------\n\nFor this formative\, you will be required to:\n\n \n\n*
  Base your work on your ALU missions (Required)\n\n======Expected to help 
 you Formulate your submission======\n\n* Identify A sector for your projec
 t (your ALU mission)\n\n* What programs within and outside ALU can I parti
 cipate in to learn more about the problem?\n\n* What kind of research do I
  need to conduct to understand the problem and the community affected bett
 er?\n\n* Arrange them in order of priority (write)\n\n* For each domain\, 
 identify 3 problems that you could offer a solution\n\n* Arrange the probl
 ems in order of importance\n\n============================================
 =========================\n\nInstructions\n------------\n\nEach student sh
 all be required to design a software solution for an ALU student-based mis
 sion. Each student shall be expected to present the problem and the sugges
 ted solution in a project proposal format.\n\nStudents shall be expected t
 o include a clear:\n\n* Description of the concept of their mission\n\n* P
 roblem statement [Include Citations]\n\n* Software development model\n\n* 
 The hypothesis of their solution\n\nMake a copy of the assignment template
  [here.] (https://docs.google.com/document/d/1E2yKyxTb6qRILZ3LOznaMTCTdRF
 cIeNP3sInCldMxLk/edit?tab=t.0)\n\nSUBMISSION REQUIREMENTS\n\nSubmit a link
  to your Google doc.\n\nMake sure to follow the naming convention on the t
 emplate. person_name_[Assignment1]_[W4]_[MMDDYYYY]\n\n \n\n \n\n*******
 ************\nAssignment 1 PART B\n*******************\n\nPROMPT\n\nFor th
 is formative\, you will be required to create an SRS document for your pro
 ject. It should have the following\;\n\n* Title of the project\n\n* All Ch
 apters in the template\n\n \n\nNOTE: This chapter structure is based on t
 he sample structure [here] (https://docs.google.com/document/d/1E2yKyxTb6q
 RILZ3LOznaMTCTdRFcIeNP3sInCldMxLk/edit?tab=t.0) (PLEASE MAKE A COPY OF THE
  TEMPLATE). However\, this is subject to change based on the content treat
 ed during the course.\n\nThe deadline for the submission of the assignment
  is on 29th September 2026 @23:59PM.\n\nSUBMISSION REQUIREMENTS\n\nSubmit 
 a link to your SRS doc.\n\nMake sure to follow the naming convention. per
 son1_name_[Assignment1]_[W4]_[MMDDYYYY]
