DESCRIPTION:Instructions\n------------\n\nDear Students\,\n\nPlease follow 
 the following Group Assignment Instructions: \n\n* Brainstorming:\n\n* Me
 et as a group and brainstorm ideas\, considering the missions/interests o
 f your group members.\n\n* Select one mission that best fits the group
 ’s collective goals.\n\n* Proposal Documentation :\n\n* Decide on a tit
 le for your project.\n\n* Use the [This Template(Make a copy)] (https://do
 cs.google.com/document/d/11hL40MR4WovPBNlh0vNNTdoFoYHseXOP/edit?usp=sharin
 g&ouid=101587096735388398746&rtpof=true&sd=true) to document the group’s
  project idea clearly.\n\n* The team leader should make a copy and complet
 e this task tracker\,  [Task Tracker] (https://docs.google.com/spreadshee
 ts/d/1XmazNYC9dsafsyL-Uj0JffcwjDaITAUv89wHFHyNvDc/edit?usp=sharing) only t
 he team leader should edit the task tracker and other members should be gi
 ven viewing access only.\n\n* Diagrams:\n\n* Each group member is responsi
 ble for creating one diagram.\n\n* The group should collectively produce 
 a set of diagrams that includes:\n\n* Structural Diagrams → Show the 
 static features of the system (e.g.\, Class Diagram\, Object Diagram\, Com
 ponent Diagram\, Deployment Diagram).\n\n* Behavioral Diagrams → Show t
 he dynamic nature of the system and interactions between objects (e.g.\, U
 se Case Diagram\, Sequence Diagram\, Activity Diagram\, State Machine Diag
 ram).\n\n* Additionally you can include a Block diagram and Flowchart.\n\n
 * Example: If your group has 7 members\, you should submit 7 diagrams i
 n total (one per member).
SEQUENCE:0
