CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:At the end of each week\, you will be required to fill out [thi
 s logbook] (https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1OZXeyN9XqA1K8il3EVX9Xy
 BCQcQguFwCgcXlLONW5lE/copy)\n\n[Links to an external site.] (https://docs.
 google.com/spreadsheets/d/19nm4qqgE5fsBgz3e93MX6DTmYjfOSsAKLP4Xf346D6Q/cop
 y?usp=sharing)\n\nThis logbook will help you and faculty keep track of the
  tasks and projects you are working on\, the amount of time you are spendi
 ng on them and the skills you are using or gaining.\n\nThe logbook will al
 so serve as a tool to help you complete your other module assessments this
  term.\n\nKindly find instructions for the logbook below.\n\nThe logbook c
 ontains three sheets: INSTRUCTIONS\, COVER PAGE\, and (COPY for more weeks
 ) WEEK 1. Here's how you can use each section effectively:\n\nINSTRUCTIONS
  Sheet\n------------------\n\n* Read Carefully: Start by reading the instr
 uctions sheet thoroughly. It will provide you with an overview of how to u
 se the logbook\, any specific guidelines set by your course\, and what is 
 expected in your entries.\n\nCOVER PAGE Sheet\n----------------\n\n* Fill 
 out ALL the cells of the COVER PAGE in your own words. DO NOT re-use the p
 oints given\; those are mere guides/examples. The total marks of the Logbo
 ok is tied to the entries of the Logbook.  If you omit or exclude one or 
 more of the cells\, you will automatically obtain less marks.\n\n \n\n(CO
 PY for more weeks) WEEK 1 Sheet\n\n* Weekly Tracking: This sheet is design
 ed for tracking your weekly activities. You'll use this format to document
  each week of your internship.\n\n* Daily Activities: For each day\, recor
 d what tasks you worked on\, the skills you utilised or developed\, and an
 y notable achievements or challenges.\n\n* Reflections: Jot down your thou
 ghts on what you've learned\, how you've grown\, and areas for improvement
 .\n\n* Feedback: In Reflecting With Composure (Reflection-in-action)\, ref
 lect and/or have a discussion with your supervisor or group members about 
 your weekly performance and document your/their insights.\n\n* Additional 
 Tasks: Be sure to document (including providing proof thereof) meetings\, 
 training sessions\, or any other special tasks assigned and completed duri
 ng the week.\n\nHow to Proceed for Subsequent Weeks\n---------------------
 --------------\n\n* Duplicate the Weekly Sheet: For each subsequent week o
 f your internship\, you should make a copy of the "WEEK 1" sheet. Rename i
 t appropriately (e.g.\, WEEK 2\, WEEK 3\, etc.) to keep your logbook organ
 ised.\n\n* Consistent Documentation: Follow the same process for each week
 \, ensuring consistency in how you document your activities\, reflections\
 , and feedback.\n\nFinal Tips\n----------\n\n* Regular Updates: Update the
  logbook at the end of each day or week to ensure accuracy and thoroughnes
 s. If you wait until the end of your internship to record your entries\, y
 ou will most assuredly have an incomplete\, basic and lacklustre Logbook!\
 n\n* Reflection and Growth: Use the reflection sections as an opportunity 
 for personal and professional growth\, critically assessing your performan
 ce and setting goals for the future.\n\nSubmission of Mid-Point Logbook As
 signment\n------------------------------------------\n\n* Mid-Point Submis
 sion: At the end of the week six of the Semester (October 27th\, at 11:59p
 m CAT)\, of your Skills Immersion 1 module\, you will submit your Mid-Poin
 t Logbook as a Microsoft Excel (.xlsx) file: not a link to your logbook in
  Google Sheet form.\n\n \n\n 
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Mid- Point Logbook [Skills_Immersion_1]
