 wn words. DO NOT re-use the points given\; those are mere guides/examples.
  The total marks of the Logbook is tied to the entries of the Logbook.&nbs
 p\; If you omit or exclude one or more of the cells\, you will automatical
 ly obtain less marks.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>&nbsp\;</strong></p
 >\n<p>(COPY for more weeks) WEEK 1 Sheet</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Weekly Tra
 cking</strong>: This sheet is designed for tracking your weekly activities
 . You'll use this format to document each week of your internship.\n<ul>\n
 <li><strong>Daily Activities</strong>: For each day\, record what tasks yo
 u worked on\, the skills you utilised or developed\, and any notable achie
 vements or challenges.</li>\n<li><strong>Reflections</strong>: Jot down yo
 ur thoughts on what you've learned\, how you've grown\, and areas for impr
 ovement.</li>\n<li><strong>Feedback</strong>: In Reflecting With Composure
  (Reflection-in-action)\, reflect and/or have a discussion with your super
 visor or group members about your weekly performance and document your/the
 ir insights.</li>\n<li><strong>Additional Tasks</strong>: Be sure to docum
 ent (including providing proof thereof) meetings\, training sessions\, or 
 any other special tasks assigned and completed during the week.</li>\n</ul
 >\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>How to Proceed for Subsequent Weeks</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><
 strong>Duplicate the Weekly Sheet</strong>: For each subsequent week of yo
 ur internship\, you should make a copy of the "WEEK 1" sheet. Rename it ap
 propriately (e.g.\, WEEK 2\, WEEK 3\, etc.) to keep your logbook organised
 .</li>\n<li><strong>Consistent Documentation</strong>: Follow the same pro
 cess for each week\, ensuring consistency in how you document your activit
 ies\, reflections\, and feedback.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Final Tips</h3>\n<ul>\n
 <li><strong>Regular Updates</strong>: Update the logbook at the end of eac
 h day or week to ensure accuracy and thoroughness. <strong>If you wait unt
 il the end of your internship to record your entries\, you will most assur
 edly have an incomplete\, basic and lacklustre Logbook!</strong></li>\n<li
 ><strong>Reflection and Growth</strong>: Use the reflection sections as an
  opportunity for personal and professional growth\, critically assessing y
 our performance and setting goals for the future.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Submiss
 ion of Mid-Point Logbook Assignment</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Mid-Point Submission: 
 <em>At the end of the week six of the Semester <strong>(October 27th</stro
 ng></em><strong>\, at 11:59pm CAT</strong><strong><em>)</em></strong><em>\
 , of your Skills Immersion 1 module\, you will submit your Mid-Point Logbo
 ok as a Microsoft Excel (.xlsx) file: <u>not a link to your logbook in Goo
 gle Sheet form. </u></em></li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp\;</p>\n<p>&nbsp\;</p>
END:VEVENT
